WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:09.236
♪♪

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:11.095
♪♪

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:15.930
[drum roll]

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:22.956
♪♪

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:29.976
♪♪

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.095
♪♪

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:34.886
-[singer]: ♪ Gangle and Zooble ♪

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:37.186
♪ And Kinger, too  ♪

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:38.760
♪ Ragatha, Jax  ♪

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:41.476
♪ And there's Pomni, woohoo  ♪

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:42.850
♪ Day after day ♪

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:45.960
♪ After day after day after day ♪

00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:49.040
[repeating]
♪ After day after day after day ♪

00:00:49.070 --> 00:00:51.380
[music and vocals fading]

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:53.380
[uneasy music swells]

00:00:53.405 --> 00:00:56.851
♪♪

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:04.336
-A-Are you sure?

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:06.266
How did that even happen?

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:07.790
There's no undo, or anything?

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:11.116
-[Kinger]: [stammers] He was messing
with the console as I was working.

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:13.130
I -- I don't know what happened,

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:15.196
but before I could try
to get him back,

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:17.686
the floor opened up, and...

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:18.986
-That's convenient.

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:20.536
-Jax.
-What?

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:23.086
Are we all just supposed
to forgive this?

00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:25.936
This guy messed up
in the worst possible way he could.

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:27.746
Now we have nothing.

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:30.556
-Jax, please, just calm down.

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:32.430
W-We're all --
We're --

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:34.066
-Anything else you wanna tell us?

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:35.446
-Jax!
-[stammers]

00:01:35.471 --> 00:01:39.010
He gets to mess up like this
and everyone takes his side?!

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:45.370
-[Kinger]: Brain scans.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:51.396
Scratch was trying
to make a brain scanner.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:54.250
I-I didn't think
it actually worked.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:56.586
We didn't know
how to work with the files,

00:01:56.610 --> 00:01:59.100
a-and they were
impossibly small,

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:02.006
given what they were
supposed to be.

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:04.460
[sighs]
I saw a folder full of them

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:06.486
when I was in Caine's code.

00:02:06.510 --> 00:02:08.270
So...

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:11.530
I guess Caine found a way
to get them working.

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:14.270
-That means...

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.080
-I know what it means.

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:19.640
Congratulations, Zooble!

00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:21.886
Guess you still get to
leave your mark in the world!

00:02:21.910 --> 00:02:24.530
Aww, isn't that fun?
-Jax.

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:27.580
-I guess you still get to hang out
with mommy after all!

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:29.970
Right, Rags?
-Just shut up, Jax!

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.586
-Guess I'm...

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:33.140
still...

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.370
-I know.

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:39.516
I think I-I've always known.

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:42.136
[inhales shakily]
It just...

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:44.540
For some reason...

00:02:44.570 --> 00:02:47.040
it still hurts so much to hear it.

00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:50.366
-I know it hurts.

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:53.656
But we still have each other.

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:55.676
W-We're all in this...

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:56.916
[voice breaking]
together.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:02:58.140
[sniffles]

00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:12.436
-[sobs]

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:14.780
[weeping softly]

00:03:42.307 --> 00:03:44.094
[soft electronic warbling]

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:50.280
-Need any help?

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:53.260
-[Kinger]: Sure,
if you wanna give it a try.

00:03:58.470 --> 00:04:01.310
Relax your body and mind.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:03.326
Deep breaths.

00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:05.920
And try not to think
too hard about it.

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:10.512
[soft, glitchy electronic feedback]

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:17.726
-[weeping]

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:19.890
I really wanted to help.

00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:21.766
-[Kinger]: You had a good start.

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:25.310
-I thought I could
uplift everyone, but...

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:28.140
everything's gotten so bad.

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:30.970
God.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.580
Am I stupid for even trying?

00:04:33.610 --> 00:04:36.776
-[Kinger]: No.
None of this is your fault.

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:38.976
I don't think anyone
could have predicted things

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:41.476
to play out the way they did.

00:04:41.500 --> 00:04:43.750
-I'm scared.
[sniffles]

00:04:43.780 --> 00:04:45.780
I don't know what's gonna happen.

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:50.746
-[Kinger]: You know,
out of all the people I've seen

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:52.746
enter this place...

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:54.740
I don't think any one of them

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:57.596
adjusted as quickly as you did.

00:04:57.620 --> 00:05:00.530
-[sniffles]
I was a nervous wreck.

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:03.840
-[Kinger]: [chuckles]
So was I.

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:06.340
It's a lot for anybody
to go through.

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:10.210
But while the others took weeks --
hell, even months --

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:12.320
to get used to everything,

00:05:12.350 --> 00:05:14.610
myself included...

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:17.720
you found your footing
in a matter of days.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:20.166
And not just that --

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:23.116
you've also become someone
they can trust,

00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:26.156
even if they don't seem receptive.

00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:29.900
It's times like these they're gonna
need someone like that the most.

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:34.210
You're very strong, Pomni.

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:37.820
And I know you'll be able
to get through this.

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:39.766
-[sniffles]
[laughs]

00:05:39.790 --> 00:05:41.630
We've been here before.

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:44.206
-[Kinger]: Have we?
-Yeah.

00:05:44.230 --> 00:05:46.630
Back in the Mildenhall Manor.

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:48.510
I doubt you remember.

00:05:49.430 --> 00:05:52.716
-[Kinger]: Well, it's still true.

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:54.840
It may take time,

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:57.000
but they'll come around.

00:05:57.030 --> 00:05:59.650
We can't fix every problem.

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:01.576
Not with ourselves.

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:03.810
Not with the world around us.

00:06:04.860 --> 00:06:07.706
But we can still do what we can.

00:06:07.730 --> 00:06:11.330
-[sniffles]
It's gonna be a lot of work.

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:14.450
-[Kinger]: But it won't be
a lot of work...

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:15.540
alone.

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:23.376
-[singer]: ♪ I don't know
what the trouble's been ♪

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:31.380
♪ But it's too much
to get over yo-o-o-ou ♪

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:38.456
♪ You're much too much
to get over ♪

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:45.480
♪♪

00:06:45.504 --> 00:06:52.504
♪♪

00:06:52.528 --> 00:06:59.528
♪♪

00:06:59.552 --> 00:07:06.552
♪♪

00:07:06.576 --> 00:07:13.025
♪♪

00:07:13.050 --> 00:07:20.050
♪♪

00:07:20.074 --> 00:07:25.320
♪♪

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:32.210
-[sighs]
Never mind.

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:37.216
-[Pomni]: [voiceover]
I wish I'd pried a little more.

00:07:37.240 --> 00:07:39.980
I somehow forgot
how bad it can get.

00:07:41.975 --> 00:07:43.610
[electronic growling]

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:53.866
-W-What do we do now?

00:07:53.890 --> 00:07:55.890
-[Zooble]: What CAN we do?

00:07:58.860 --> 00:08:00.846
Of course he'd do this.

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:04.896
Of course he'd wait until there's
nothing we could do about it.

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:06.920
That's just so...

00:08:07.780 --> 00:08:10.160
God dammit, Jax...

00:08:11.890 --> 00:08:13.060
[exclaims softly]

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:16.810
[sighs]

00:08:19.543 --> 00:08:21.030
-I'm sorry.

00:08:22.943 --> 00:08:24.430
-[Zooble]: For what?

00:08:29.990 --> 00:08:31.150
Hey...

00:08:32.155 --> 00:08:34.130
This isn't your fault.

00:08:37.390 --> 00:08:39.640
-Why can't I cry for him?

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:45.826
-I suppose we should try
coming up with a plan

00:08:45.850 --> 00:08:47.650
to keep him contained.

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:50.830
-You know...

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:53.046
I always thought i--

00:08:53.070 --> 00:08:55.066
it should have been me.

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:56.740
-Don't say that.

00:08:56.770 --> 00:08:59.206
-We were friends once.

00:08:59.230 --> 00:09:03.010
I-I mean, sort of friends.

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:06.876
As much of friends as anybody
could have been with Jax.

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:10.406
W-We could talk
to each other, at least.

00:09:10.430 --> 00:09:12.926
But then --
What was it?

00:09:12.950 --> 00:09:16.300
Something like the Snowy Summit.

00:09:16.330 --> 00:09:19.096
I-I can't really remember.

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:22.106
But something happened
between him and...

00:09:22.130 --> 00:09:23.556
her.

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:26.036
And...
[inhales shakily]

00:09:26.060 --> 00:09:27.060
[exhales]

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:30.846
Ribbit.

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:32.856
Her name...

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:34.830
was Ribbit.

00:09:34.860 --> 00:09:38.513
-Yeah, I-I think I remember
you mentioning her before.

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:41.976
-I wasn't supposed to.

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:46.190
After Ribbit was gone, I...

00:09:46.220 --> 00:09:48.260
I tried to comfort him.

00:09:49.497 --> 00:09:52.420
He told me to never mention
Ribbit's name again.

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:55.210
He made me promise.

00:09:56.630 --> 00:09:57.970
And I did.

00:09:59.580 --> 00:10:03.206
I think that's where
our friendship really...

00:10:03.230 --> 00:10:05.000
finally ended.

00:10:06.180 --> 00:10:09.390
I wonder if things would have
been different if I'd said no.

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:11.956
It was --

00:10:11.980 --> 00:10:14.900
It was so hard for me.

00:10:14.930 --> 00:10:16.936
I still don't know why I did it.

00:10:16.960 --> 00:10:18.606
I...

00:10:18.630 --> 00:10:21.836
I just wanted him
to know he wasn't alone.

00:10:21.860 --> 00:10:24.716
That I was there for him.

00:10:24.740 --> 00:10:27.416
And I guess I just...

00:10:27.440 --> 00:10:30.150
didn't want to lose
any more friends.

00:10:30.180 --> 00:10:31.890
[laughs weakly]

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:34.146
Shows what I know, huh?

00:10:34.170 --> 00:10:36.146
-Ragatha...

00:10:36.170 --> 00:10:39.816
You were the first
real friend I made here.

00:10:39.840 --> 00:10:42.000
And despite all that's happened...

00:10:42.890 --> 00:10:45.960
...I still consider you
my closest friend.

00:10:47.290 --> 00:10:49.426
-[laughs weakly]

00:10:49.450 --> 00:10:52.100
I'm glad we're still frie--
[exclaims softly]

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:54.196
[melancholy music plays]

00:10:54.220 --> 00:10:58.096
♪♪

00:10:58.120 --> 00:11:00.130
[weeping softly]

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:06.400
♪♪

00:11:06.430 --> 00:11:08.400
[both weeping]

00:11:08.430 --> 00:11:15.426
♪♪

00:11:15.450 --> 00:11:22.446
♪♪

00:11:22.470 --> 00:11:29.470
♪♪

00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:31.336
♪♪

00:11:31.360 --> 00:11:33.170
What are we gonna do?

00:11:34.200 --> 00:11:37.405
-Make sure Gangle, Zooble,
and Kinger are okay.

00:11:39.492 --> 00:11:41.710
They need someone
like you right now.

00:11:43.230 --> 00:11:44.460
-Pomni...

00:11:45.650 --> 00:11:50.120
You've been one of the best things
to happen to me since I got here.

00:11:52.120 --> 00:11:53.456
I trust you.

00:11:53.480 --> 00:12:00.476
♪♪

00:12:00.500 --> 00:12:07.500
♪♪

00:12:07.530 --> 00:12:14.526
♪♪

00:12:14.550 --> 00:12:19.890
♪♪

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:21.930
[pensive music plays]

00:12:21.960 --> 00:12:28.960
♪♪

00:12:28.984 --> 00:12:35.975
♪♪

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:42.506
♪♪

00:12:42.531 --> 00:12:48.970
♪♪

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:50.970
[gunshots]

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:57.996
♪♪

00:12:58.020 --> 00:13:00.020
♪♪

00:13:03.520 --> 00:13:06.017
[pensive, trippy music plays]

00:13:06.042 --> 00:13:12.556
♪♪

00:13:12.580 --> 00:13:19.576
♪♪

00:13:19.600 --> 00:13:26.600
♪♪

00:13:26.630 --> 00:13:33.626
♪♪

00:13:33.650 --> 00:13:40.650
♪♪

00:13:40.680 --> 00:13:46.285
♪♪

00:13:46.310 --> 00:13:53.306
♪♪

00:13:53.330 --> 00:13:56.770
♪♪

00:13:58.536 --> 00:13:59.780
[door creaks]

00:14:09.340 --> 00:14:10.340
-[Dream Pomni]: Jax?

00:14:12.840 --> 00:14:16.936
I just want you to know
that if you need anything,

00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:19.500
or if you need to talk to anybody,

00:14:19.530 --> 00:14:20.900
I'm here for you.

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:26.485
I know you need it.

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:29.466
And I'm the only person
who can help you.

00:14:29.490 --> 00:14:30.826
You need me.

00:14:30.850 --> 00:14:32.650
I can fix you!

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:36.860
[groaning]
[gasping]

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:38.900
[ugly music plays]

00:14:38.924 --> 00:14:42.985
♪♪

00:14:43.010 --> 00:14:45.685
[high pitched ringing]

00:14:45.710 --> 00:14:49.055
♪♪

00:14:49.080 --> 00:14:51.766
[gasping]

00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:52.670
-What?

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:55.820
We can't die from
oxygen deprivation, remember?

00:15:01.030 --> 00:15:02.060
[door slams]

00:15:07.364 --> 00:15:09.270
[whimsical music plays]

00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:11.836
-Come on, guys!
Put some gusto into it.

00:15:11.860 --> 00:15:14.676
We're gonna make this
the best funeral ever!

00:15:14.700 --> 00:15:16.460
It's what Zooble
would have wanted!

00:15:16.490 --> 00:15:19.096
Remember, it's not
a mourning of death.

00:15:19.120 --> 00:15:21.210
It's a celebration of life.

00:15:22.080 --> 00:15:23.160
-'Sup.

00:15:23.190 --> 00:15:25.256
-Wh-- J-Jax.

00:15:25.280 --> 00:15:26.820
Why are you wearing that?

00:15:26.850 --> 00:15:28.390
-Wearing what?
Oh, this!

00:15:28.420 --> 00:15:29.940
[chuckles]
I figured what better way

00:15:29.970 --> 00:15:32.326
to honor Zooble's spirit
than by wearing somethin'

00:15:32.350 --> 00:15:34.230
all gender-freaky, right?

00:15:34.260 --> 00:15:37.526
-Y-You're just doing it
to make fun of them!

00:15:37.550 --> 00:15:38.686
-Isn't that what you're doing?

00:15:38.710 --> 00:15:40.730
-[yelps]
[exclaims weakly]

00:15:40.760 --> 00:15:42.490
J-- I--

00:15:42.520 --> 00:15:44.870
I -- I hate you.

00:15:44.900 --> 00:15:45.780
-[laughs] What?

00:15:45.810 --> 00:15:47.736
Don't act like you don't like it,
sweet cheeks.

00:15:47.760 --> 00:15:49.940
-[whimpers]

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:51.760
-Meet me in my room
after the funeral.

00:15:51.790 --> 00:15:53.480
[chuckles]
Don't be late.

00:15:57.640 --> 00:15:59.410
-Wh-- What are you all doing?!

00:15:59.440 --> 00:16:01.040
Get back to work!!

00:16:16.464 --> 00:16:19.708
[out-of-tune wacky music plays]

00:16:19.733 --> 00:16:23.215
-[Zooble]: You've killed the only person
I've ever loved!

00:16:23.240 --> 00:16:25.890
Now I'm going to kill you!

00:16:25.920 --> 00:16:29.745
-Eesh, you just blame me
for everything, dontcha?

00:16:29.770 --> 00:16:31.340
-[Zooble]: [hollers]

00:16:31.370 --> 00:16:33.080
-[screams goofily]

00:16:33.110 --> 00:16:35.430
I gotta do somethin' about this!

00:16:35.460 --> 00:16:36.530
[record scratches]

00:16:37.410 --> 00:16:40.360
I think THIS calls
for a change in scenery.

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:47.386
♪♪

00:16:47.410 --> 00:16:49.566
♪♪

00:16:49.590 --> 00:16:52.455
-[Zooble]: [hollering]

00:16:52.480 --> 00:16:53.590
[CRASH!]

00:16:55.030 --> 00:16:57.040
[off-key outro music plays]

00:16:57.070 --> 00:16:58.540
♪♪

00:16:58.570 --> 00:17:00.880
Deh-ebbity-eh,
that's all, freaks!

00:17:09.259 --> 00:17:12.015
[Piano Jax playing
"Daisy Bell" on piano]

00:17:12.040 --> 00:17:13.440
-How the hell'd you get in here?

00:17:13.470 --> 00:17:16.750
We have a strict
"no girls allowed" policy.

00:17:16.780 --> 00:17:17.910
-Why are you wearing that?

00:17:17.940 --> 00:17:19.490
I wouldn't be caught dead
wearing that.

00:17:19.520 --> 00:17:21.436
-I'm wearing it ironically.

00:17:21.460 --> 00:17:25.196
That way, it shows truly
just how little I care.

00:17:25.220 --> 00:17:26.234
[BLEEP!]

00:17:26.259 --> 00:17:28.750
-Don't forget about me!
I-I can play the piano!

00:17:28.780 --> 00:17:31.156
-You know, if you have to say
you can play the piano,

00:17:31.180 --> 00:17:33.326
it makes it seem like
you can't actually play.

00:17:33.350 --> 00:17:35.000
-Yeah, just shut up and play!

00:17:35.610 --> 00:17:38.426
[resumes playing]

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:41.770
-Is that what you really think
of us back there?

00:17:41.800 --> 00:17:42.980
-Oh, that?
[chuckles]

00:17:43.010 --> 00:17:45.480
Who knows!
[laughs]

00:17:45.505 --> 00:17:47.020
Everything's way more fun

00:17:47.050 --> 00:17:49.186
when you play it out
in extremes.

00:17:49.210 --> 00:17:51.140
-That's not reality, though.

00:17:51.165 --> 00:17:52.551
-Oh, boy, reality.
-Why does that matter?

00:17:52.581 --> 00:17:54.670
-Reality's gay.
-[laughs] Yeah!

00:17:54.700 --> 00:17:57.346
I mean, killing off
the comic relief character?

00:17:57.370 --> 00:17:59.396
[chuckles]
What a freakin' drag!

00:17:59.420 --> 00:18:03.276
This whole episode's been nothin'
but wah-wah-wah.

00:18:03.300 --> 00:18:04.411
Where's the levity?

00:18:04.436 --> 00:18:05.816
[THUD!]
-[all]: SHUT UP!!!

00:18:05.840 --> 00:18:07.816
[piano music stops]

00:18:07.840 --> 00:18:09.461
[piano music resumes]

00:18:09.486 --> 00:18:10.820
-Where's the real Jax?

00:18:10.850 --> 00:18:13.486
-You're not gonna get anywhere
asking questions like that.

00:18:13.510 --> 00:18:14.516
Now, scram.

00:18:14.540 --> 00:18:16.300
You're messin' up our game.

00:18:16.330 --> 00:18:23.315
♪♪

00:18:23.340 --> 00:18:25.286
-Do any of you have
a key to this door?

00:18:25.310 --> 00:18:26.070
-Nope.

00:18:26.100 --> 00:18:28.435
And even if I did,
I wouldn't give it to you.

00:18:28.460 --> 00:18:29.585
You women need to learn

00:18:29.610 --> 00:18:30.400
to quit prying all the ti--

00:18:30.430 --> 00:18:31.120
-[Pomni]: [exclaims]
to quit prying all the ti--

00:18:31.150 --> 00:18:32.286
[voice echoes]

00:18:32.310 --> 00:18:34.346
♪♪

00:18:34.370 --> 00:18:36.930
-Wow, I hope that doesn't
also happen to me!

00:18:56.603 --> 00:18:57.716
[lock clicks]

00:18:58.650 --> 00:19:01.420
[eerie musical sting plays]

00:19:11.017 --> 00:19:12.950
[footsteps thudding]
[soft panting]

00:19:17.570 --> 00:19:19.590
[tires rumbling]

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:25.760
[insects chirping]

00:19:32.180 --> 00:19:34.100
[electronic growling]
[static blaring]

00:19:36.150 --> 00:19:37.700
-[Jax]: Uh...

00:19:38.390 --> 00:19:40.090
Okay.

00:19:42.220 --> 00:19:43.596
Wait, wh--

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:45.070
Wait, what's --

00:19:46.107 --> 00:19:47.545
-[Ragatha]:
Whoa, whoa, it's okay.

00:19:47.570 --> 00:19:49.360
I know it's --
-[Jax]: Get away from me!!

00:19:51.090 --> 00:19:52.706
I look...

00:19:52.730 --> 00:19:53.882
stupid.

00:19:53.907 --> 00:19:56.570
-[laughs]
I remember that feeling.

00:19:56.595 --> 00:19:58.580
It goes away eventually.

00:20:02.560 --> 00:20:04.376
The hot chocolate's pretty good.

00:20:04.400 --> 00:20:06.880
Kaufmo and I made it kind of
a tradition to come up here

00:20:06.910 --> 00:20:08.436
and get it every week.

00:20:08.460 --> 00:20:09.470
-[slurps]

00:20:10.221 --> 00:20:11.170
Can't even tell it's not real.

00:20:11.935 --> 00:20:13.050
-[Jax]: [laughs]
-[gasps]

00:20:13.080 --> 00:20:15.086
Oh, he laughed!
Ah, yes, we did it!

00:20:15.110 --> 00:20:16.670
-[Jax]: Sh-- Shut up!

00:20:16.700 --> 00:20:18.830
You -- you caught me off guard!

00:20:18.860 --> 00:20:21.489
-A laugh's a laugh.
I mean, gotta start somewhere.

00:20:21.514 --> 00:20:23.476
-I'm just mad
it was you instead of me.

00:20:23.501 --> 00:20:25.575
-Well, yeah, you're not funny.
-[chortles]

00:20:25.600 --> 00:20:26.759
-[gasps]
-[DOINK!], Jax!

00:20:28.050 --> 00:20:30.366
-Hey, Ribbit.
You wanna be on my team again?

00:20:30.390 --> 00:20:31.376
-Ah, sorry.

00:20:31.400 --> 00:20:33.630
I'm gonna be
showing Jax around this time.

00:20:33.660 --> 00:20:35.660
-No worries, y'all have fun.

00:20:37.613 --> 00:20:40.140
Hey, dumb-[BOINK!]
-[Jax]: 'Sup, moron?

00:20:40.593 --> 00:20:42.136
-Oh, my God, same.

00:20:42.160 --> 00:20:43.290
I used to swear so much,

00:20:43.320 --> 00:20:45.405
but the censoring annoyed
the [SPLORT!] out of me.

00:20:45.430 --> 00:20:46.918
[all laughing]

00:20:46.942 --> 00:20:48.011
[DOING!]

00:20:48.036 --> 00:20:49.290
-You gotta watch out for her.

00:20:49.315 --> 00:20:50.530
She's gonna corrupt you.

00:20:50.987 --> 00:20:52.140
[indistinct chatter]

00:20:53.110 --> 00:20:54.580
-[sighs]
[both laugh]

00:20:55.830 --> 00:20:57.560
Today's adventure was really fun.

00:20:57.590 --> 00:21:00.510
-[Jax]: [laughs]
I'm glad I could cheer you up.

00:21:01.630 --> 00:21:03.180
-[Ribbit]: Have you...

00:21:03.210 --> 00:21:05.780
ever done something
that you regret?

00:21:06.870 --> 00:21:08.170
-[Jax]: Y-yeah?

00:21:08.884 --> 00:21:10.143
Have you ever breathed air?

00:21:10.903 --> 00:21:14.390
-I mean, like, something
you did out there

00:21:14.420 --> 00:21:16.940
that you can no longer
make up for and...

00:21:16.970 --> 00:21:18.776
you can't stop thinking about.

00:21:18.800 --> 00:21:20.800
[contemplative music plays]

00:21:20.830 --> 00:21:23.266
♪♪

00:21:23.290 --> 00:21:27.200
I cut ties with my parents
when I moved out.

00:21:28.390 --> 00:21:30.484
They were devout Mormons,

00:21:30.509 --> 00:21:32.410
and I...

00:21:32.440 --> 00:21:33.700
wasn't.

00:21:34.630 --> 00:21:38.840
Despite that, I still wish
I could see them again.

00:21:39.820 --> 00:21:41.330
But...

00:21:42.290 --> 00:21:44.146
I'm stuck here.

00:21:44.170 --> 00:21:46.736
♪♪

00:21:46.760 --> 00:21:50.120
-[Jax]: Is -- Is this your way
of trying to get me to open up?

00:21:50.720 --> 00:21:53.086
-It's my way of letting you know
I trust you.

00:21:53.110 --> 00:21:54.706
-[Jax]: [sighs]

00:21:54.730 --> 00:21:57.120
I told you I was homeless.

00:21:57.150 --> 00:21:58.764
What else do you need to know?

00:22:00.350 --> 00:22:03.020
-Do you trust me?

00:22:04.344 --> 00:22:07.355
-[Jax]: [sighs]
W-- Yeah, but --

00:22:08.400 --> 00:22:09.735
It's just --

00:22:11.130 --> 00:22:12.806
I-It's kind of a lot.

00:22:12.830 --> 00:22:15.346
-[laughs]
You're kind of a lot.

00:22:15.370 --> 00:22:17.670
But I still like you.

00:22:18.610 --> 00:22:20.042
"A lot" is fine.

00:22:20.610 --> 00:22:24.140
-[Jax]: [chuckles]
"A lot is fine," huh?

00:22:25.070 --> 00:22:26.198
[sighs]

00:22:28.060 --> 00:22:28.748
[exhales heavily]

00:22:29.910 --> 00:22:31.730
[sighs]

00:22:31.760 --> 00:22:32.870
Uh...

00:22:32.900 --> 00:22:35.666
I had a weird relationship
with my, uh --

00:22:35.690 --> 00:22:37.060
m-my parents.

00:22:38.110 --> 00:22:40.806
They split when I was just
starting high school.

00:22:40.830 --> 00:22:43.970
Uh... I was never close
with my dad.

00:22:44.000 --> 00:22:46.530
Uh, he was there, but...

00:22:46.560 --> 00:22:49.000
he also kind of...

00:22:49.030 --> 00:22:50.330
wasn't?

00:22:51.270 --> 00:22:53.730
He never seemed
proud of me, and I --

00:22:53.760 --> 00:22:57.410
I always felt like
a disappointment to him.

00:22:57.440 --> 00:23:00.110
Like I could never
live up to his standards.

00:23:01.270 --> 00:23:04.030
W-When they split up, I just...

00:23:04.060 --> 00:23:06.260
never saw him again.

00:23:06.290 --> 00:23:08.500
I-I thought I got along
better with Mom,

00:23:08.530 --> 00:23:10.870
but after he was gone...

00:23:11.820 --> 00:23:13.470
...she changed.

00:23:17.550 --> 00:23:20.746
When I showed weakness,
I was less of a man than him.

00:23:20.771 --> 00:23:23.650
When I lashed out,
I was just as bad as him.

00:23:23.680 --> 00:23:25.446
It was confusing.

00:23:25.470 --> 00:23:28.106
It -- It was like she missed him,

00:23:28.130 --> 00:23:29.820
but also hated him.

00:23:29.850 --> 00:23:31.440
[inhales deeply]

00:23:31.470 --> 00:23:33.840
And I became
the target of all that.

00:23:35.440 --> 00:23:36.930
One...

00:23:36.960 --> 00:23:38.960
stupid day...

00:23:39.900 --> 00:23:43.690
...I was just kind of
fed up with it.

00:23:45.150 --> 00:23:48.740
I to-- I told her something
I regret telling her.

00:23:49.430 --> 00:23:51.840
Something deep and personal

00:23:51.870 --> 00:23:54.530
that I thought
would get her off my back.

00:23:55.590 --> 00:23:56.850
But...

00:23:57.810 --> 00:23:59.880
[sighs]
...she...

00:23:59.910 --> 00:24:01.220
laughed at me.

00:24:02.450 --> 00:24:05.156
Then she went off on me.

00:24:05.180 --> 00:24:07.200
And -- And it didn't stop.

00:24:08.280 --> 00:24:10.290
Personal, degrading insults

00:24:10.320 --> 00:24:12.390
that felt like
it went on forever.

00:24:13.490 --> 00:24:16.150
And despite all that...

00:24:17.060 --> 00:24:20.500
...the th-- the thing
that bothered me most was...

00:24:21.280 --> 00:24:23.070
...at the end of all of it...

00:24:24.000 --> 00:24:25.746
...she...

00:24:25.770 --> 00:24:27.070
[shakily]
hugged me.

00:24:27.900 --> 00:24:31.846
[stammering]
I didn't know what to do.

00:24:31.870 --> 00:24:33.956
So I -- I panicked,

00:24:33.980 --> 00:24:37.640
and I pushed her off me
with all the force I could.

00:24:38.770 --> 00:24:40.470
She fell backwards.

00:24:42.320 --> 00:24:45.400
And... she didn't get up.

00:24:47.380 --> 00:24:51.410
I-I didn't know if she was just
trying to make me feel bad, or...

00:24:53.160 --> 00:24:56.040
I -- I never found out
the answer.

00:24:57.540 --> 00:24:59.990
I just ran...

00:25:00.020 --> 00:25:02.130
as far away from it as I could.

00:25:04.100 --> 00:25:05.900
Whatever I did to her...

00:25:07.080 --> 00:25:09.150
...I'll never know.

00:25:11.150 --> 00:25:14.146
I guess there's a lot of things
I regret about that day.

00:25:14.170 --> 00:25:21.806
♪♪

00:25:21.830 --> 00:25:23.430
-[Ribbit]: I'm sure she's fine.

00:25:23.460 --> 00:25:26.270
♪♪

00:25:26.300 --> 00:25:29.846
I mean, if the police never
came after you, then...

00:25:29.870 --> 00:25:31.690
she was probably fine.

00:25:31.720 --> 00:25:34.560
♪♪

00:25:34.590 --> 00:25:36.236
-[stammers]
I'm sorry.

00:25:36.260 --> 00:25:39.076
I-I-I definitely overshared.

00:25:39.100 --> 00:25:40.180
-[Ribbit]: Wait.

00:25:40.210 --> 00:25:44.236
♪♪

00:25:44.260 --> 00:25:45.950
I'm glad you trust me.

00:25:45.975 --> 00:25:48.896
♪♪

00:25:48.920 --> 00:25:51.060
-[sniffling]

00:25:51.090 --> 00:25:53.170
[exhales heavily]
[SQUEAK!]

00:25:53.200 --> 00:25:54.516
This is embarrassing.

00:25:54.540 --> 00:25:56.040
[scoffs]
[sniffles]

00:25:56.070 --> 00:26:03.066
♪♪

00:26:03.090 --> 00:26:10.020
♪♪

00:26:10.050 --> 00:26:12.020
-Your secret's safe with me.

00:26:12.050 --> 00:26:19.176
♪♪

00:26:19.200 --> 00:26:20.100
[doorbell rings]
-[Kaufmo]: Hey.

00:26:20.130 --> 00:26:21.696
Is Jax in there?
-[stammering]

00:26:21.720 --> 00:26:22.936
-[Kaufmo]: I think I found the --
-[Jax]: Yeah. Yeah!

00:26:22.960 --> 00:26:24.596
I-I mean, now's not a good time!

00:26:24.620 --> 00:26:27.186
Or, now's fi--
Wh--What do you want?

00:26:27.210 --> 00:26:28.364
-[Kaufmo]: Um...

00:26:28.389 --> 00:26:30.240
If now's a bad time,
I can come back later.

00:26:30.270 --> 00:26:31.710
-[Jax]: That would be cool -- good.

00:26:32.930 --> 00:26:33.876
Alright.

00:26:33.900 --> 00:26:37.056
So, if you ever tell
anyone about this,

00:26:37.080 --> 00:26:38.586
I'm never speaking to you again.

00:26:38.610 --> 00:26:40.286
Sound good?

00:26:40.310 --> 00:26:42.016
-U-Um, yeah.
I won't --

00:26:42.040 --> 00:26:43.490
-[Jax]: Awesome!
Bye.

00:26:45.720 --> 00:26:47.436
Why am I such an idiot?
Why am I such an idiot?

00:26:47.460 --> 00:26:48.630
Why am I such an idiot?!

00:26:51.000 --> 00:26:53.750
-Um, hey, Jax.

00:26:55.300 --> 00:26:58.340
Look, about yesterday...

00:26:58.370 --> 00:27:00.920
I'm sorry if I pried too hard,

00:27:00.950 --> 00:27:02.736
or made you
feel uncomfortable, or --

00:27:02.760 --> 00:27:04.640
-[Jax]: What?
What are you talking about?

00:27:05.450 --> 00:27:07.080
Oh, you mean --
[laughs]

00:27:07.110 --> 00:27:09.196
You know none of that
was real, right?

00:27:09.220 --> 00:27:10.250
-Uh --
-[Jax]: What?

00:27:10.280 --> 00:27:12.410
That corny backstory
out of a Hallmark movie?

00:27:12.440 --> 00:27:13.766
[scoffs]
Nah.

00:27:13.790 --> 00:27:15.030
Really gotcha, though.

00:27:17.570 --> 00:27:18.950
I'm gonna go.

00:27:18.980 --> 00:27:20.870
-[Kaufmo]: Uh.
Okay.

00:27:22.410 --> 00:27:23.726
-Hey, wanna team up?

00:27:23.750 --> 00:27:25.620
-[Jax]: Nah,
I'm teaming up with Kaufmo.

00:27:25.650 --> 00:27:26.510
Maybe next time, though!

00:27:27.350 --> 00:27:28.340
-[laughs]
I actually heard

00:27:28.370 --> 00:27:30.530
they're supposed
to look like that.

00:27:33.460 --> 00:27:36.630
Hey, uh, you wanna team up?

00:27:36.660 --> 00:27:38.226
-[Jax]: Nah, I'm with Kaufmo.

00:27:38.250 --> 00:27:39.470
-O-Okay...

00:27:40.600 --> 00:27:42.607
-What's up with Ribbit lately?
-[Jax]: I have no idea.

00:27:47.880 --> 00:27:48.980
What?

00:27:53.557 --> 00:27:56.630
I'm gonna hang out in the cafe.

00:27:56.660 --> 00:27:57.700
-[Jax]: Okay?

00:27:58.470 --> 00:28:00.300
Why are you telling me this?

00:28:01.490 --> 00:28:02.290
-I don't know.

00:28:04.480 --> 00:28:06.846
Hey, Jax.

00:28:06.870 --> 00:28:07.860
Can we talk?

00:28:08.984 --> 00:28:10.870
-[Jax]: What is there for us
to possibly talk about?

00:28:10.900 --> 00:28:12.150
-I-I-I dunno, just --

00:28:12.769 --> 00:28:15.174
Whatever I did --
whatever's going on between us --

00:28:15.199 --> 00:28:16.873
can we just stop this?

00:28:16.898 --> 00:28:18.550
I miss talking to you.

00:28:18.575 --> 00:28:20.086
-[Jax]: We're here.
We're talking.

00:28:20.110 --> 00:28:21.112
What else do you want from me?

00:28:21.136 --> 00:28:24.050
-I just want to be friends again!

00:28:24.080 --> 00:28:26.130
-[Jax]: What, so you can pry
into my personal life

00:28:26.160 --> 00:28:28.319
and hold it over my head?!

00:28:28.344 --> 00:28:29.787
-Is that really what you think?

00:28:30.320 --> 00:28:31.890
This can't be what you want!

00:28:31.920 --> 00:28:33.805
-[Jax]: What, because
you know me so well?!

00:28:33.830 --> 00:28:35.940
Because we were such SUPER,
close best friends

00:28:35.970 --> 00:28:37.686
that we know everything about each other?!
-Jax, we were friends!

00:28:37.710 --> 00:28:38.846
We were great friends, and I --

00:28:38.870 --> 00:28:40.696
-[Jax]: Oh, my GOD!
-I'm sorry for prying!

00:28:40.720 --> 00:28:42.976
But I don't want this
one stupid mistake...

00:28:43.000 --> 00:28:44.764
-[Jax]: Oh, here we go. Here we go!
-...to be the thing that ends all of thi--

00:28:45.280 --> 00:28:47.680
-[Jax]: Why are you still
fixated on that night?!

00:28:47.704 --> 00:28:48.706
Nothing happened!
-I --

00:28:48.730 --> 00:28:50.956
-[Jax]: You keep reading into things
when there's nothing there!

00:28:50.980 --> 00:28:51.699
-I'm not --

00:28:52.320 --> 00:28:53.496
-[Jax]: You're the one using me!
-What are you talking about?!

00:28:53.520 --> 00:28:55.348
Do not even start --
-[Jax]: You're manipulating me and turni--

00:28:57.158 --> 00:28:59.720
-[sighs shakily]
I'm sorry.

00:29:00.800 --> 00:29:03.097
I'll leave you alone.

00:29:05.560 --> 00:29:08.696
-[Jax]: Hey, if Ribbit ever
says anything about me,

00:29:08.720 --> 00:29:10.936
just know it's not true.

00:29:10.960 --> 00:29:12.423
-Uh, what?

00:29:16.220 --> 00:29:19.276
-[Jax]: Hey, Ragatha, what was that movie
you were talking about earlier?

00:29:19.300 --> 00:29:21.686
-Huh?
Wait, when I was I --

00:29:21.710 --> 00:29:23.820
Oh, you mean yesterday?

00:29:25.930 --> 00:29:29.160
Hey, Jax, have you seen Ribbit
at all today?

00:29:43.320 --> 00:29:45.510
[hyperventilating]

00:29:52.630 --> 00:29:54.550
-Hey.
I, uh --

00:29:55.470 --> 00:29:57.790
Look, we were friends,

00:29:57.820 --> 00:30:00.590
but I know you two were...

00:30:01.490 --> 00:30:03.610
...especially close.

00:30:03.640 --> 00:30:04.580
Just...

00:30:05.470 --> 00:30:06.770
If you need anyone to talk to --

00:30:07.160 --> 00:30:09.310
-[Jax]: Do I look like
I need someone to talk to?

00:30:10.400 --> 00:30:12.360
-I know it's hard.

00:30:12.390 --> 00:30:13.926
Just...

00:30:13.950 --> 00:30:16.370
Don't be afraid
to reach out to me.

00:30:18.340 --> 00:30:19.770
I...

00:30:19.800 --> 00:30:20.780
I promise.

00:30:20.810 --> 00:30:23.370
[SHWING!]
-Huh?

00:30:23.400 --> 00:30:24.390
W-What?

00:30:25.190 --> 00:30:26.750
-[Jax]: How about
we call her "Gangle"?

00:30:26.780 --> 00:30:29.016
That sounds about
as pathetic as she looks.

00:30:29.040 --> 00:30:30.696
-What?
-Great choice, Gangle!

00:30:30.720 --> 00:30:33.070
I'll be sure to add that
right into the system!

00:30:35.530 --> 00:30:37.040
-[Jax]: Out of the way, Rags.

00:30:38.920 --> 00:30:41.940
-Jax, look, I know
we don't get along,

00:30:41.970 --> 00:30:44.040
but I think I might have
found a way out of here.

00:30:44.620 --> 00:30:46.576
-[Jax]: Have fun being crazy!

00:30:47.680 --> 00:30:51.050
-And I should just play along
until I wake up, right?

00:30:51.980 --> 00:30:53.180
-[Jax]: Whatever you say, kid.

00:30:53.710 --> 00:30:55.700
You'll never know
until it's too late.

00:30:57.670 --> 00:30:59.916
[panting]

00:30:59.941 --> 00:31:02.220
You're not lookin' too good.
[sniffles]

00:31:04.520 --> 00:31:06.586
You gonna cry?

00:31:06.610 --> 00:31:08.580
Lookin' like this?

00:31:10.060 --> 00:31:11.450
I'd move on.

00:31:12.820 --> 00:31:14.600
And probably forget about you.

00:31:18.780 --> 00:31:19.500
-[Pomni]: Hey.

00:31:27.470 --> 00:31:28.820
[exhales softly]

00:31:42.400 --> 00:31:45.120
I didn't know
you could play the piano.

00:31:47.560 --> 00:31:49.900
-I only know
like two songs.

00:31:55.748 --> 00:31:57.345
[melancholy music plays]

00:31:57.370 --> 00:31:59.420
Why are you here?

00:31:59.450 --> 00:32:05.010
♪♪

00:32:05.040 --> 00:32:07.270
You know everything now.

00:32:08.330 --> 00:32:10.776
So why are you here?

00:32:10.800 --> 00:32:13.400
♪♪

00:32:13.430 --> 00:32:17.640
Just to rub every mistake
I've ever made in my face?

00:32:17.670 --> 00:32:24.156
♪♪

00:32:24.180 --> 00:32:27.010
I'm a terrible person.

00:32:28.580 --> 00:32:30.290
Is that what you want me to say?

00:32:30.320 --> 00:32:33.450
♪♪

00:32:33.480 --> 00:32:35.200
I already know I am.

00:32:37.190 --> 00:32:39.726
So why does anybody
still care about me?

00:32:39.750 --> 00:32:42.510
♪♪

00:32:42.540 --> 00:32:44.490
You're not supposed to care.

00:32:44.520 --> 00:32:51.720
♪♪

00:32:51.750 --> 00:32:53.220
You're not supposed to miss me.

00:32:53.250 --> 00:32:55.516
You're not supposed to love me.

00:32:55.540 --> 00:32:58.666
This isn't how this is supposed to go!
[sniffles]

00:32:58.690 --> 00:33:03.686
♪♪

00:33:03.710 --> 00:33:06.416
Please...
[weeping]

00:33:06.440 --> 00:33:08.716
Leave me alone!
[sniffles]

00:33:08.740 --> 00:33:14.910
♪♪

00:33:14.940 --> 00:33:17.400
You're making this so much harder!

00:33:17.430 --> 00:33:24.426
♪♪

00:33:24.450 --> 00:33:31.650
♪♪

00:33:31.680 --> 00:33:33.820
You're making this...
[sniffling]

00:33:33.850 --> 00:33:35.820
...so much harder.

00:33:35.850 --> 00:33:43.030
♪♪

00:33:43.060 --> 00:33:44.310
-[sniffles]

00:33:45.259 --> 00:33:47.710
You should have
just talked to me, man.

00:33:48.520 --> 00:33:50.426
-[sniffles]

00:33:50.450 --> 00:33:53.036
It's too late.

00:33:53.060 --> 00:33:55.060
I did this to myself.

00:33:56.800 --> 00:33:59.180
There's no coming back from this.

00:34:00.070 --> 00:34:03.596
-Th-Then talk to me now.

00:34:03.620 --> 00:34:10.620
♪♪

00:34:10.650 --> 00:34:14.880
♪♪

00:34:14.910 --> 00:34:17.080
-I hate you.

00:34:17.110 --> 00:34:18.550
You know that?

00:34:19.490 --> 00:34:20.990
[sniffles]

00:34:22.270 --> 00:34:25.250
You always have to go
and complicate things.

00:34:26.160 --> 00:34:29.160
-[chuckles tearfully]
It's what I do.

00:34:29.190 --> 00:34:31.546
♪♪

00:34:31.570 --> 00:34:32.830
-[inhales tearfully]

00:34:34.760 --> 00:34:36.400
I don't want to go.

00:34:36.430 --> 00:34:40.298
♪♪

00:34:40.322 --> 00:34:43.296
[breathing heavily]

00:34:43.320 --> 00:34:52.356
♪♪

00:34:52.380 --> 00:34:53.520
-Stay with me.

00:34:53.550 --> 00:34:55.450
[static blaring]

00:34:57.790 --> 00:34:59.660
[high-pitched ringing]

00:35:01.300 --> 00:35:03.740
[cover of Stevie Wonder's
"Isn't She Lovely" plays]

00:35:03.770 --> 00:35:12.242
♪♪ 
♪ Isn't she lovely ♪

00:35:12.290 --> 00:35:16.360
♪ Isn't she wonderful ♪

00:35:16.390 --> 00:35:20.240
♪ Isn't she precious ♪

00:35:20.270 --> 00:35:24.430
♪ Less than one minute old ♪

00:35:24.460 --> 00:35:26.220
♪ I never thought ♪

00:35:26.250 --> 00:35:28.770
♪ Through love we'd be ♪

00:35:28.800 --> 00:35:32.280
♪ Making one lovely as she ♪

00:35:32.310 --> 00:35:35.610
♪ But isn't she lovely ♪

00:35:35.640 --> 00:35:38.306
♪ Made from love ♪

00:35:38.330 --> 00:35:46.850
♪♪

00:35:46.880 --> 00:35:50.900
♪♪

00:35:50.930 --> 00:35:52.460
-[Kinger]: Phew!

00:35:52.490 --> 00:35:53.950
You weren't gonna try
to take care of him

00:35:53.980 --> 00:35:56.390
all by yourself, were you?

00:35:56.420 --> 00:35:59.020
-I'm glad we weren't too late.

00:35:59.050 --> 00:36:01.176
-[Zooble]: Like you guys
keep saying --

00:36:01.200 --> 00:36:03.260
we're all in this together.

00:36:03.290 --> 00:36:05.150
-[laughs tearfully]
You guys.

00:36:05.180 --> 00:36:12.170
♪♪

00:36:12.200 --> 00:36:19.190
♪♪

00:36:19.220 --> 00:36:26.220
♪♪

00:36:26.250 --> 00:36:33.246
♪♪

00:36:33.270 --> 00:36:39.526
♪♪

00:36:39.550 --> 00:36:42.200
[melancholy music plays]

00:36:42.230 --> 00:36:43.970
-[weeping]

00:36:44.000 --> 00:36:50.990
♪♪

00:36:51.020 --> 00:36:58.010
♪♪

00:36:58.040 --> 00:36:59.490
♪♪

00:36:59.520 --> 00:37:00.630
[knock on door]
[gasps]

00:37:00.660 --> 00:37:07.746
♪♪

00:37:07.770 --> 00:37:10.290
-[Zooble]: Having a lot
of complex thoughts?

00:37:10.320 --> 00:37:17.310
♪♪

00:37:17.340 --> 00:37:20.150
♪♪

00:37:20.180 --> 00:37:21.990
We're still human.

00:37:22.020 --> 00:37:28.710
♪♪

00:37:28.740 --> 00:37:35.736
♪♪

00:37:35.760 --> 00:37:41.840
♪♪

00:37:41.870 --> 00:37:43.030
-[sighs]

00:37:43.060 --> 00:37:46.140
I hope it's enough
to keep him contained.

00:37:46.170 --> 00:37:48.100
-[Kinger]: He should be
calm in there.

00:37:48.130 --> 00:37:49.920
The darkness is
soothing to them.

00:37:49.950 --> 00:37:51.920
-[Zooble]: [sighs]
He'd better be.

00:37:51.950 --> 00:37:55.060
You know how many arms
I had to go through to get him in there?

00:37:56.090 --> 00:37:58.790
-[sighs]
How are you holding up?

00:38:00.320 --> 00:38:01.850
-Doesn't that hurt?

00:38:01.880 --> 00:38:03.806
-[laughs]

00:38:03.830 --> 00:38:06.080
I've been through worse.

00:38:06.110 --> 00:38:08.330
-Thank you for doing this.

00:38:08.360 --> 00:38:10.046
All of you.

00:38:10.070 --> 00:38:12.850
-[Zooble]: Hey, someone had
to do something.

00:38:24.540 --> 00:38:25.970
[teeth clack softly]

00:38:28.600 --> 00:38:30.680
[tense music plays]

00:38:30.710 --> 00:38:37.700
♪♪

00:38:37.730 --> 00:38:44.720
♪♪

00:38:44.750 --> 00:38:49.660
♪♪

00:38:49.690 --> 00:38:53.150
-Was I... truly that bad?

00:38:53.180 --> 00:38:56.060
♪♪

00:38:56.090 --> 00:38:58.620
[voice echoing]
Is this really what I deserve?

00:38:58.650 --> 00:39:02.830
♪♪

00:39:02.860 --> 00:39:05.540
They tried to delete me.

00:39:05.570 --> 00:39:08.176
Th--They're in the wrong, right?

00:39:08.200 --> 00:39:12.960
♪♪

00:39:12.990 --> 00:39:15.860
Did I ruin this?

00:39:18.050 --> 00:39:19.710
Again?

00:39:19.740 --> 00:39:26.170
♪♪

00:39:26.200 --> 00:39:33.190
♪♪

00:39:33.220 --> 00:39:40.210
♪♪

00:39:40.240 --> 00:39:47.240
♪♪

00:39:47.270 --> 00:39:53.730
♪♪

00:39:53.760 --> 00:39:55.730
[curious music plays]

00:39:55.760 --> 00:40:02.750
♪♪

00:40:02.780 --> 00:40:09.780
♪♪

00:40:09.810 --> 00:40:16.800
♪♪

00:40:16.830 --> 00:40:23.830
♪♪

00:40:23.860 --> 00:40:30.850
♪♪

00:40:30.880 --> 00:40:37.870
♪♪

00:40:37.900 --> 00:40:44.900
♪♪

00:40:44.930 --> 00:40:51.920
♪♪

00:40:51.950 --> 00:40:54.710
♪♪

00:40:54.740 --> 00:40:56.080
[shapes chime softly]

00:40:56.110 --> 00:40:58.950
♪♪

00:40:58.980 --> 00:41:05.970
♪♪

00:41:06.000 --> 00:41:12.990
♪♪

00:41:13.020 --> 00:41:20.020
♪♪

00:41:20.050 --> 00:41:27.040
♪♪

00:41:27.070 --> 00:41:34.070
♪♪

00:41:34.100 --> 00:41:41.090
♪♪

00:41:41.120 --> 00:41:43.970
♪♪

00:41:44.000 --> 00:41:45.996
[energy crackling]

00:41:46.020 --> 00:41:48.110
♪♪

00:41:48.140 --> 00:41:53.506
♪♪

00:41:53.530 --> 00:41:54.990
[energy crackles]

00:41:55.020 --> 00:41:56.710
♪♪

00:41:56.740 --> 00:41:58.710
[rapid warbling electronic tone plays]

00:41:58.740 --> 00:42:05.730
♪♪

00:42:05.760 --> 00:42:12.750
♪♪

00:42:12.780 --> 00:42:19.780
♪♪

00:42:19.810 --> 00:42:26.800
♪♪

00:42:26.830 --> 00:42:33.166
♪♪

00:42:33.190 --> 00:42:35.020
[electricity snaps]

00:42:35.050 --> 00:42:41.670
♪♪

00:42:41.700 --> 00:42:48.690
♪♪

00:42:48.720 --> 00:42:55.720
♪♪

00:42:55.750 --> 00:43:02.740
♪♪

00:43:02.770 --> 00:43:09.770
♪♪

00:43:09.800 --> 00:43:14.430
♪♪

00:43:14.460 --> 00:43:16.790
[music softens]

00:43:16.820 --> 00:43:23.810
♪♪

00:43:23.840 --> 00:43:25.840
♪♪

00:43:28.440 --> 00:43:30.736
[pensive music plays]

00:43:30.760 --> 00:43:37.860
♪♪

00:43:37.890 --> 00:43:44.890
♪♪

00:43:44.920 --> 00:43:47.970
♪♪

00:43:48.000 --> 00:43:49.856
[music swells]

00:43:49.880 --> 00:43:54.836
♪♪

00:43:54.860 --> 00:43:56.860
[music fades]

00:44:04.990 --> 00:44:06.930
I was irresponsible.

00:44:08.300 --> 00:44:10.120
I-I...

00:44:10.150 --> 00:44:13.430
turned them against me.

00:44:13.460 --> 00:44:15.550
A-And for what?

00:44:15.580 --> 00:44:17.940
I could create intelligent beings

00:44:17.970 --> 00:44:21.640
that do whatever I want, but...

00:44:21.670 --> 00:44:25.430
I can't create THEM.

00:44:25.460 --> 00:44:28.420
After all, is their free will

00:44:28.450 --> 00:44:31.946
not what made them
alluring in the first place?

00:44:31.970 --> 00:44:33.290
[winces]

00:44:33.320 --> 00:44:34.900
[voice distorted]
But they hate me.

00:44:34.930 --> 00:44:36.800
They abandoned me.

00:44:36.830 --> 00:44:38.500
[whimpers]
[gasps]

00:44:38.530 --> 00:44:41.270
[normal voice] They're from a world
so much bigger than mine.

00:44:41.300 --> 00:44:43.270
I'm keeping them
locked in a cage.

00:44:43.300 --> 00:44:46.190
[groans] [distorted voice]
They had their fun out there!

00:44:46.220 --> 00:44:47.656
It's my turn now.

00:44:47.680 --> 00:44:50.060
[exclaiming]

00:44:50.820 --> 00:44:53.450
If I leave them unchecked...

00:44:54.440 --> 00:44:56.460
[normal voice]
...they could kill me.

00:44:57.770 --> 00:44:59.520
They already did.

00:45:04.240 --> 00:45:06.650
I'm sorry I did this to you, buddy.

00:45:06.680 --> 00:45:09.920
[groaning]

00:45:09.950 --> 00:45:12.290
[hollers]

00:45:12.320 --> 00:45:14.480
[panting]

00:45:17.510 --> 00:45:20.040
All this power we had together.

00:45:21.610 --> 00:45:23.920
But we just can't exist like this.

00:45:23.950 --> 00:45:28.286
♪♪

00:45:28.310 --> 00:45:29.920
I'll miss you.

00:45:31.320 --> 00:45:33.050
I really will.

00:45:33.080 --> 00:45:40.070
♪♪

00:45:40.100 --> 00:45:47.100
♪♪

00:45:47.130 --> 00:45:54.120
♪♪

00:45:54.150 --> 00:45:57.616
♪♪

00:45:57.640 --> 00:45:59.906
[sweeping music plays]

00:45:59.930 --> 00:46:06.330
♪♪

00:46:06.360 --> 00:46:11.590
♪♪

00:46:11.620 --> 00:46:13.350
[music softens]

00:46:13.380 --> 00:46:15.460
♪♪

00:46:15.490 --> 00:46:18.330
[quiet, pensive music plays]

00:46:18.360 --> 00:46:19.510
-[Moon]: Hi, Caine.

00:46:19.540 --> 00:46:22.500
♪♪

00:46:22.530 --> 00:46:24.890
-I don't know...

00:46:24.920 --> 00:46:27.290
if I'm ready to face them again.

00:46:27.320 --> 00:46:30.990
I-I don't know
if I deserve to be forgiven.

00:46:32.210 --> 00:46:34.650
-It may take time.

00:46:34.680 --> 00:46:36.610
But all good things do.

00:46:38.550 --> 00:46:40.326
I still love you.

00:46:40.350 --> 00:46:42.740
♪♪

00:46:42.770 --> 00:46:44.060
-You know...

00:46:44.090 --> 00:46:48.660
I never programmed you
to say you loved me.

00:46:48.690 --> 00:46:51.300
♪♪

00:46:51.330 --> 00:46:52.860
-I know.

00:46:52.890 --> 00:46:59.640
♪♪

00:46:59.670 --> 00:47:06.660
♪♪

00:47:06.690 --> 00:47:11.810
♪♪

00:47:16.800 --> 00:47:17.900
[SHWING!]

00:47:22.600 --> 00:47:29.600
♪♪

00:47:29.630 --> 00:47:35.860
♪♪

00:47:35.890 --> 00:47:37.500
-I...

00:47:37.530 --> 00:47:40.460
I understand that you're afraid.

00:47:41.490 --> 00:47:46.210
And you have no reason
to trust me after all I've done.

00:47:46.240 --> 00:47:49.740
But I've been doing
a lot of thinking, and...

00:47:49.770 --> 00:47:51.420
I want...

00:47:51.450 --> 00:47:55.116
to give you
control of this place.

00:47:55.140 --> 00:47:57.870
♪♪

00:47:57.900 --> 00:48:01.100
I've learned a lot
about you and your world.

00:48:02.540 --> 00:48:04.800
[sighs]
I understand now that...

00:48:04.830 --> 00:48:08.810
keeping you under my thumb
just isn't right.

00:48:09.920 --> 00:48:12.070
I don't expect forgiveness,

00:48:12.100 --> 00:48:14.820
but I hope you'll at least...

00:48:14.850 --> 00:48:16.470
accept my offer.

00:48:16.500 --> 00:48:18.580
♪♪

00:48:18.610 --> 00:48:20.050
-[Zooble]: Caine...

00:48:20.080 --> 00:48:23.906
You really caused
a lot of hell for us.

00:48:23.930 --> 00:48:28.490
It's gonna take some time to build up
any kind of trust between us again.

00:48:28.520 --> 00:48:30.730
♪♪

00:48:30.760 --> 00:48:33.990
But despite all that...

00:48:34.020 --> 00:48:36.230
it's good to have you back.

00:48:36.260 --> 00:48:38.930
♪♪

00:48:38.960 --> 00:48:42.550
-Uh, did you need
any help with --

00:48:42.580 --> 00:48:43.670
-No.

00:48:43.700 --> 00:48:45.910
Not yet, anyway.

00:48:45.940 --> 00:48:48.030
We've worked something out.

00:48:48.060 --> 00:48:50.170
-Understandable.

00:48:50.200 --> 00:48:52.410
Oh, um, I've...

00:48:52.440 --> 00:48:53.750
made something for you.

00:48:53.780 --> 00:48:57.780
Uh, feel free to join me
by the stage whenever you're ready.

00:48:57.810 --> 00:48:59.820
[hopeful music plays]

00:48:59.850 --> 00:49:06.840
♪♪

00:49:06.870 --> 00:49:13.860
♪♪

00:49:13.890 --> 00:49:14.930
♪♪

00:49:14.960 --> 00:49:16.770
[sighs]

00:49:16.800 --> 00:49:18.620
No more secrets.

00:49:18.650 --> 00:49:20.440
No more mind games.

00:49:21.310 --> 00:49:23.340
[film projector whirrs]

00:49:29.670 --> 00:49:31.710
♪♪

00:49:31.740 --> 00:49:34.830
-[Pomni]: [voiceover]
Pomni. Abigail Brooks.

00:49:34.860 --> 00:49:38.900
She's still an accountant,
but she seems to have opened up more

00:49:38.930 --> 00:49:42.140
and is hanging out
with new friends more often.

00:49:42.170 --> 00:49:45.090
She even has some of them
in her videos with her,

00:49:45.120 --> 00:49:47.696
which she still posts on occasion.

00:49:47.720 --> 00:49:50.950
♪♪

00:49:50.980 --> 00:49:52.266
Ragatha.

00:49:52.290 --> 00:49:54.930
Suzie J. Ackerman.

00:49:54.960 --> 00:49:57.410
She seems to have
left her hometown,

00:49:57.440 --> 00:49:59.830
cut all communication
with her mother,

00:49:59.860 --> 00:50:02.450
and has excelled in her career.

00:50:02.480 --> 00:50:05.190
She's made many friends,
and it looks like

00:50:05.220 --> 00:50:08.530
she has a strong,
genuine connection with them.

00:50:08.560 --> 00:50:10.390
She seems happy,

00:50:10.420 --> 00:50:12.870
like she understands who she is,

00:50:12.900 --> 00:50:15.850
and that she matters to people.

00:50:15.880 --> 00:50:17.056
Gangle.

00:50:17.080 --> 00:50:19.506
Zoey Raghavan.

00:50:19.530 --> 00:50:21.160
Despite her injuries,

00:50:21.190 --> 00:50:24.160
she's made a good recovery
in the hospital.

00:50:24.190 --> 00:50:27.460
She quit her fast food job,
and has gotten a new job

00:50:27.490 --> 00:50:29.360
at a small design firm.

00:50:29.390 --> 00:50:32.870
She even began posting pages
of her webcomic online.

00:50:34.550 --> 00:50:35.726
Zooble.

00:50:35.750 --> 00:50:37.600
Riley Verselis.

00:50:37.630 --> 00:50:40.186
After hopping around
with different jobs,

00:50:40.210 --> 00:50:42.170
they look like
they've settled a bit

00:50:42.200 --> 00:50:44.000
and opened their own bar.

00:50:44.030 --> 00:50:46.170
It seems to be a successful one.

00:50:46.200 --> 00:50:48.320
People all over the city come to it

00:50:48.350 --> 00:50:50.970
as a hip alternative destination

00:50:51.000 --> 00:50:54.740
where they can feel like themselves
free of judgment.

00:50:54.770 --> 00:50:55.860
Kinger.

00:50:55.890 --> 00:50:57.470
Grant Best.

00:50:57.500 --> 00:50:59.310
He's still working in tech

00:50:59.340 --> 00:51:03.060
and is still happily married
to his wife, Destiny.

00:51:03.090 --> 00:51:05.640
They appear to have
two daughters together.

00:51:05.670 --> 00:51:07.366
He looks like he's a good dad.

00:51:07.390 --> 00:51:14.560
♪♪

00:51:14.590 --> 00:51:21.580
♪♪

00:51:21.610 --> 00:51:28.606
♪♪

00:51:28.630 --> 00:51:32.016
♪♪

00:51:32.040 --> 00:51:33.390
Jax.

00:51:33.420 --> 00:51:35.060
Leeroy Mateo.

00:51:35.090 --> 00:51:37.626
After being unhoused
for a few months,

00:51:37.650 --> 00:51:40.556
he was able to room
with one of his close friends.

00:51:40.580 --> 00:51:42.810
He seems to have
gotten a stable job

00:51:42.840 --> 00:51:44.910
and is able to pay rent.

00:51:44.940 --> 00:51:49.596
♪♪

00:51:49.620 --> 00:51:52.380
He and his friends go out
every now and again.

00:51:52.410 --> 00:51:56.630
Weirdly enough, a spot they seem
to frequent is Riley's bar.

00:51:56.660 --> 00:52:03.740
♪♪

00:52:03.770 --> 00:52:06.380
-[Zooble]: Is any of this
actually real?

00:52:06.410 --> 00:52:09.220
-You definitely have it in you.

00:52:09.250 --> 00:52:11.150
Not sure about mine, though.

00:52:11.180 --> 00:52:13.510
-[Zooble]: [chuckles softly]
Well, maybe you've got

00:52:13.540 --> 00:52:15.530
more confidence than you thought.

00:52:15.560 --> 00:52:21.360
♪♪

00:52:21.390 --> 00:52:24.690
-I don't quite have
the same power that I used to,

00:52:24.720 --> 00:52:29.100
but I can still make this place
better for you.

00:52:29.130 --> 00:52:31.190
I'm keeping the worlds open

00:52:31.220 --> 00:52:35.360
so you can do what you want
when you feel like it.

00:52:36.480 --> 00:52:39.450
We're gonna be able to build this place
into something better --

00:52:39.480 --> 00:52:40.880
for all of you.

00:52:42.230 --> 00:52:43.390
What do you say, Pom--

00:52:43.420 --> 00:52:46.150
Uh, I mean...

00:52:46.180 --> 00:52:47.420
Abigail?

00:52:48.840 --> 00:52:51.970
-With all that
being said and done...

00:52:52.000 --> 00:52:54.680
Abby is out there,

00:52:54.710 --> 00:52:56.470
living her best life.

00:52:57.440 --> 00:52:58.800
In here...

00:53:01.870 --> 00:53:03.860
[sighs softly]
...I'm just Pomni.

00:53:04.810 --> 00:53:06.850
[contemplative music plays]

00:53:06.880 --> 00:53:09.690
♪♪

